cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DSNI, please cite the manuscript below and the upstream databases listed in docs/dependencies.md."
title: "DSNI: Recommending Bacterial Cultivation Conditions from 16S rRNA"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-25"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24524177
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Q9gJYx/AI4DSNI"
abstract: >-
  DSNI pairs one 16S rRNA gene sequence per bacterial strain with four cultivation
  conditions (growth medium, temperature, pH, oxygen requirement) drawn from BacDive,
  MediaDive and NCBI, with a genus-disjoint train/val/test split, a scripted rebuild, and
  baseline models up to a Transformer with a biological variability gate.
keywords:
  - 16S rRNA
  - bacterial cultivation
  - dataset
  - benchmark
  - multi-task learning
